#. Diagram label
msgid "A Knowledge Graph, a root URL, a CDN target"
msgstr ""

#: processes/process/render-kg-to-cdn.bpmn:92
#. Diagram label
msgid "another CDN"
msgstr ""

#: processes/process/render-kg-to-cdn.bpmn:51
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Answered by the target just determined and the Tool registry. GitHub Pages runs bootstrap-tools\\' process by name. Another CDN whose Tool satisfies `render-kg-to-cdn` runs that Tool\\'s own process, which a higher layer owns (a Cloudflare publish, for one), so this layer cannot name it. No Tool for the target reports not-pushed and names the missing Tool, rather than guessing a mechanism."
msgstr ""

#: processes/process/render-kg-to-cdn.bpmn:64
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "BOUND BY THE TOOL, so no `calledElement` is written here, and only on this branch: the CDN is not GitHub Pages, and its Tool, which a higher layer owns (a Cloudflare publish, for one), lists the process this descends into. A lower layer cannot name a higher layer\\'s process. Whatever the Tool, it returns the same status and message."
msgstr ""

#: processes/process/render-kg-to-cdn.bpmn:58
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "BOUND BY THE TOOL, so no `calledElement` is written here: the `gh-pages` Tool lists the process this descends into, render-kg-to-github-pages, and that process is held by a layer cat-harness does not need, so naming it would bind upward. What it does: make sure gh-pages exists and Pages serves it, stage, check the staging, commit onto gh-pages, check what is served. It returns the status and the message Task_Report records."
msgstr ""

#: processes/process/render-kg-to-cdn.bpmn:28
#. Diagram label
